0,Ligurian language (ancient) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ligurian_language_(ancient),"The Ligurian language was an ancient Indo-European language [4] spoken by the Ligures, an indigenous people of north-western Italy and south-eastern France in pre-Roman and Roman times. No continuous text in the language survives: Ligurian is known almost entirely through place and river names, tribal and personal names, and a few glosses quoted by Greek and Latin authors. The single most ...",Ligurian,Indo-European
1,Ligures - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ligures,"A French school, following d'Arbois de Jubainville and Camille Jullian, made Ligurian an Indo-European language intermediate between Celtic and Italic, while an Italian school stressed a deep pre-Indo-European ""Mediterranean"" stratum beneath a thinner Indo-European one.",Ligurian,Indo-European
2,The Sound of Indo-European Music (Compilation) - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgHSW774Q-4,"In this video, I compiled music from all the major Indo-European languages. I hope you enjoy these great songs!",Ligurian,Indo-European
3,LIGURIANI (Suoni dai Mondi Liguri) | LIGURIANI | ITALY ROOTS MUSIC,https://italyrootsmusic.bandcamp.com/album/liguriani-suoni-dai-mondi-liguri,"LIGURIANI present a show in which, words and sounds, evoke images and sentiments of culture and history of Liguria. Setting out right from the lantern of Genoa, place of departure and longed return, representing ""home"" for Ligurian people, for an imaginary journey that takes us through Liguria old snapshots revealing customs, traditions and themes of this people, squeezed between steep ...",Ligurian,Indo-European
4,Indoeuropean Rhythm - Thomas Fitz-Hugh - Google Books,https://books.google.com/books/about/Indoeuropean_Rhythm.html?id=ARIa0AEACAAJ,"This groundbreaking study explores the connections between Indo-European languages and the rhythms of human speech and music. Drawing on a wide range of sources, including linguistic theory, mythology, and anthropology, this book offers a compelling vision of the role of language and music in human culture.This work has been selected by scholars as being culturally important, and is part of ...",Ligurian,Indo-European
5,Indo-european Musical Idiom and Indo-european Ethnogenesis,https://www.academia.edu/79042915/INDO_EUROPEAN_MUSICAL_IDIOM_AND_INDO_EUROPEAN_ETHNOGENESIS,"The parallels outside the Indo-European cultural range show possible Uralic and Caucasian components of Indo-European musical idiom, which may indicate components of ethnogenesis of Indo-European ethnic groups. Thus ethnomusicology may be regarded as an independent source for studying prehistory, along with linguistics, archeology, and genetics.",Ligurian,Indo-European
6,Kingdoms of the Ligures - Ligurians - The History Files,https://www.historyfiles.co.uk/KingListsEurope/BarbarianLigurians.htm,"The Ligurian coastline of modern Italy owes its name to the Ligurian people, a pre-Indo-European grouping which probably consisted of several influences prior to being Latinised by the Romans",Ligurian,Indo-European
7,Traditional Ligurian Music: I Liguriani - Wandering Italy Blog,https://www.wanderingitaly.com/blog/article/1098/traditional-ligurian-music-i-liguriani,"Video of I Liguriani, a group that plays traditional Ligurian music, playing in the 11th century Church of San Andrea in Levanto in Liguria.",Ligurian,Indo-European
